<http://data.silknow.org/object/ec10404e-163b-35db-a525-2ce44981094a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This fragment of cream satin was painted in China for the export market. Silks such as these were used both as furnishing fabrics and as dress material. The marks around the edges indicate that this piece was used for upholstery. Unlike dye, paint does not penetrate into the fibres of the fabric and so easily rubs off, so this would not have been a very durable material."@en , "Upholstery fragment of painted silk, China, ca. 1780-1800"@en , "Upholstery fragment of white satin-weave silk painted in delicate shades of blue, pink, purple, green and tan with fairly large detatched flower sprays, interspersed with smaller springs."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1936e7ae-788e-3317-8258-372d04b40394> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Upholstery fragment of painted silk, China, ca. 1780-1800"@en , "Upholstery fragment of white satin-weave silk painted in delicate shades of blue, pink, purple, green and tan with fairly large detatched flower sprays, interspersed with smaller springs."@en , "This fragment of cream satin was painted in China for the export market. Silks such as these were used both as furnishing fabrics and as dress material. The marks around the edges indicate that this piece was used for upholstery. Unlike dye, paint does not penetrate into the fibres of the fabric and so easily rubs off, so this would not have been a very durable material."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/ec10404e-163b-35db-a525-2ce44981094a/dimension/3> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/ec10404e-163b-35db-a525-2ce44981094a/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/ec10404e-163b-35db-a525-2ce44981094a/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/ec10404e-163b-35db-a525-2ce44981094a/dimension/1> ;
